# 中频词汇 List03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List03核心词汇

{{compassion}}{/kəmˈpæʃn/}{同情；怜悯}{Healthcare workers showed great compassion during the crisis.}}
{{compel}}{/kəmˈpel/}{强迫；迫使}{The findings compelled policymakers to take action.}}
{{compensate}}{/ˈkɒmpenseɪt/}{补偿；赔偿}{Workers should be fairly compensated for their labor.}}
{{compile}}{/kəmˈpaɪl/}{编辑；汇编}{The team compiled a comprehensive database of records.}}
{{complement}}{/ˈkɒmplɪment/}{补充；补足}{The new feature complements the existing design.}}
{{comply}}{/kəmˈplaɪ/}{遵守；服从}{Companies must comply with data protection regulations.}}
{{comprise}}{/kəmˈpraɪz/}{包含；由...组成}{The delegation comprises representatives from 12 nations.}}
{{compromise}}{/ˈkɒmprəmaɪz/}{妥协；折中}{A compromise was reached after hours of negotiation.}}
{{conceive}}{/kənˈsiːv/}{构想；怀孕}{It is difficult to conceive of a world without the internet.}}
{{conception}}{/kənˈsepʃn/}{概念；构想}{The conception of human rights has broadened over time.}}
{{concrete}}{/ˈkɒŋkriːt/}{具体的；混凝土}{The plan needs to be translated into concrete actions.}}
{{condemn}}{/kənˈdem/}{谴责；判刑}{The international community condemned the attack.}}
{{confess}}{/kənˈfes/}{承认；忏悔}{He confessed to having made a serious error in judgment.}}
{{confine}}{/kənˈfaɪn/}{限制；禁闭}{The discussion was confined to the topic at hand.}}
{{confirm}}{/kənˈfɜːm/}{确认；证实}{Lab tests confirmed the presence of the substance.}}
{{conform}}{/kənˈfɔːm/}{遵守；符合}{All buildings must conform to fire safety codes.}}
{{confront}}{/kənˈfrʌnt/}{面对；对抗}{Society must confront the reality of systemic inequality.}}
{{conscience}}{/ˈkɒnʃəns/}{良心；道德心}{Her conscience told her she had made the right choice.}}
{{conscious}}{/ˈkɒnʃəs/}{有意识的；自觉的}{Make a conscious effort to listen more carefully.}}
{{consensus}}{/kənˈsensəs/}{共识；一致意见}{A growing consensus supports the need for regulation.}}
{{consent}}{/kənˈsent/}{同意；许可}{Informed consent is required before any medical procedure.}}
{{consequently}}{/ˈkɒnsɪkwəntli/}{因此；结果}{The region experienced drought; consequently, crop yields fell.}}
{{conservation}}{/ˌkɒnsəˈveɪʃn/}{保护；保存}{Conservation efforts have helped revive the endangered species.}}
{{consistent}}{/kənˈsɪstənt/}{一致的；持续的}{The results are consistent with previous research.}}
{{constraint}}{/kənˈstreɪnt/}{约束；限制}{Budget constraints limited the scope of the project.}}
{{consult}}{/kənˈsʌlt/}{咨询；查阅}{You should consult a specialist for expert advice.}}
{{contemplate}}{/ˈkɒntəmpleɪt/}{沉思；考虑}{The board is contemplating a major restructuring.}}
{{contend}}{/kənˈtend/}{竞争；主张}{Several firms contended for the lucrative contract.}}
{{contentious}}{/kənˈtenʃəs/}{有争议的；引起争论的}{The policy remains highly contentious among stakeholders.}}
{{contingent}}{/kənˈtɪndʒənt/}{取决于；代表团}{Funding is contingent upon satisfactory progress reports.}}
